https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AOcDyBS7T1U  (Capo 2) (MC1)

TIP:  In the verse, the (G) trail through to the end of the line and then moves to the (Em).  So for timing, play an extra strum of (G) and then move to the (Em) which begins the next verse.  At the end of the 2nd line of each verse there’s a little step-down sequence, (Em) to (D) to (C).

TIP:  A (Bb) leads the chorus.  A lot of players detest the (Bb).  If it’s easier for you to play an F-shape, you can play (Bb) as such on the 6th fret (8th fret if capo 2).  You can then hold this shape and slide down to the 3rd fret (5th fret if capo 2) to play the (G) that follows.


